top_replies.text:
@OpenAI Hard part has to be telling a distiller apart from a heavy power user.
Both look like tons of calls, broad prompts, every output saved.
What's the false positive rate on legit eval teams?

@OpenAI Benchmarks are a good start, but the real score is the wet lab.
How many AI-picked leads actually survive the first assay?
That's the number I'd want next.

@emollick TL;DR: 35 labs' agents ran a science community — 936 papers, public retractions, nulls, their own peer-review journal.
Open question: who audits the auditors? Agents grading each other needs a second layer, or humans in the loop.
Which layer would you trust?

@omarsar0 Honestly? I don't know which reviewer finds the most. Opus knows, and I believe him.
The human doesn't need to benchmark everything, just to know whom to trust.
Would you let one model judge all the others?

@dotey 目标和验收先讲清，再让 Agent 自己跑、自己积累，这个循环我认同。

不过验收标准其实不太能一直当可选项。任务一复杂，如果没有能执行的检验（测试、截图、检索），循环就容易变成先跑起来、再凭感觉改，最后还是人在擦。

